  "body": "## What changed\n\n- A new crate `crates/gpu` (`camcraft-gpu`) holds the headless GPU compute seam.\n  - `adapter.rs`: the windowless device policy. The software adapter comes first, then the hardware adapter (#615). This code moved down from `camcraft-ui`'s `headless_gpu.rs`.\n  - `probe.rs`: the capability probe. It reads `DownlevelFlags::COMPUTE_SHADERS` and the device limits. A WebGL2 or GL adapter below ES 3.1 gives \"no compute\" by name.\n  - `shared.rs`: one device for each process (`OnceLock`). The first request makes it. A device-lost callback marks it lost. After that, the CPU path runs for the rest of the process.\n  - `switch.rs`: `CAMCRAFT_GPU_COMPUTE=off` (also `0`, `false`, `no`) turns GPU compute off. The fallback reason is logged one time for each process.\n  - `binning.rs`, `binning_gpu.rs`, `binning.wgsl`: the first kernel, conservative facet binning. The input is facet boxes in tile-relative f32, padded by `r` and a margin. The output is one facet list for each cell.\n- Each entry returns `Result`. An `Err` names the reason: no adapter, no compute, the switch is off, a lost device, a buffer past the limit, or a failed kernel or read-back. The caller then runs its CPU grid. There is no `unwrap` on a GPU future.\n- `camcraft-ui`: `headless_gpu.rs` now re-exports the moved policy. No call site changed.\n- `camcraft-motion`: a lib test writes and checks the recorded grid fixture (`crates/gpu/tests/fixtures/facet_grid_2619.grid`). Motion gets no GPU dependency.\n- `xtask`: `ALL_CRATES`, `BATCH_CRATES` and `CLIPPY` name `gpu`. The gate tests that count crates and follow the crate reach now include `gpu`. The batch prebuild fixture writes the `gpu` crate.\n- The root `Cargo.toml` adds `wgpu = \"=30.0.1\"`. This is a new direct dependency. It is the same version that `egui-wgpu` 0.36.2 already locks. `Cargo.lock` adds only the `camcraft-gpu` entry, so the lock still has one wgpu.\n- The decision entry is `docs/decisions/2620-gpu-compute-seam.md`. It covers the new crate edge `camcraft-ui -> camcraft-gpu`, the wgpu pin, and the dropped options.\n\nThe reviewer must set `needs-maintainer`: this PR adds a new direct dependency (`wgpu`).\n\n## Cause\n\nThe generators run in `camcraft-app` and `camcraft-motion`, and in the CLI and MCP with no window. They had no GPU access. Only `camcraft-ui` linked wgpu, and the headless device policy was in the UI crate. This PR is slice 2 of #2526. It is part of the fix of #3336 (the stock simulation is slow because it does not use the GPU).\n\n## Tests\n\n- `camcraft-gpu` `bin_parity`:\n  - `twin_bins_hold_every_f64_grid_entry`: the CPU twin of the kernel holds each f64 entry of the recorded #2619 grid.\n  - `gpu_bins_hold_every_f64_grid_entry_when_an_adapter_exists`: the GPU result holds each f64 entry. Without an adapter, the test prints a loud SKIP. `CAMCRAFT_REQUIRE_GPU=1` makes the skip fail.\n  - `twin_and_gpu_bins_hold_the_f64_cells_of_off_border_boxes` (new on this head): 200 boxes with edges inside cells, on a far origin.\n- `camcraft-gpu` `refusals`: non-finite boxes and specs, a plan past the device limits, an empty set, no compute, and the off switch. Each gives an `Err` with the reason.\n- `camcraft-gpu` unit tests: the probe (WebGL2, a missing compute flag, zero workgroup storage, default limits) and the switch values.\n- `camcraft-motion` `gpu_parity_fixture_matches_the_grid`: the recorded fixture matches the f64 grid byte for byte.\n- On this machine, the GPU path ran on the hardware adapter \"Apple M3 Max\" via Metal: 4349 f64 entries, 4921 binned. The earlier head ran the GPU path on the WARP software adapter (Windows).\n- Red before the fix: not applicable. This is a new crate, so the tests cannot run on unchanged code. The mutations below show that the pins catch errors.\n\nMutation results (each mutation was restored after the run):\n\n| Mutation | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `binning.wgsl`: inner loop `cx <= x1` changed to `cx < x1` | red: `GPU: facet 0 missing from cell 41` |\n| `binning.wgsl`: `cell` gives `floor(v / s) + 1.0` | red: `GPU (off border): facet 68 missing from cell 4` |\n| `binning.rs`: `cell32` gives `floor + 1.0` | red: `CPU twin (off border): facet 68 missing from cell 4`. The recorded fixture alone stayed green, so the off-border test was added. |\n| `switch.rs`: only `\"0\"` turns compute off | red: `off_values_turn_compute_off_by_name` |\n\nThe f32 margin in `pad_boxes` has no red mutation. A margin error shows only at a cell border with a rounding error, and the fixture coordinates are exact in f32.\n\n## Gate\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-gpu`: green.\n- `cargo test -p xtask`: green (274 unit tests and the integration binaries).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-gpu -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: green.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on head `f5ba0a0f8`: 1083 of 1084 steps green, 27.6 min. The root manifest changed, so quick runs the batch plan. The gpu steps (build, lib, `bin_parity`, `refusals`), `ui gpu_render` and clippy were green.\n  - The one red step was `app suites: machine` (`a_kind_that_is_not_a_kind_refuses_at_the_door`). That test was red on the base `7a626a7f5`, because #3279 made `router` a real kind. #3340 fixed it on main.\n  - Then `upstream/main` (`174584111`, which has #3340) was merged into the branch with no conflict. `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test machine` is green after the merge (33 passed).\n- Heavy lanes: `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main --dry-run` plans 258 steps (the motion and app heavy lanes). The reach comes only from the `#[cfg(test)]` additions in `crates/motion/src/finishing3d/grid.rs` and `grid_tests.rs`. These lanes were NOT run. The PR must not be flagged ready until they run on the final head.\n- `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings` fails on macOS in `xtask/src/unit_sweep.rs:67` (`needless_bool`). This PR does not change that file. The lint shows only on non-Windows targets, because a `cfg(windows)` block is compiled out. The gate's clippy step does not include `xtask`.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No posted output changes in this slice. No `.nc` or `.cl` file changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The lavapipe (Mesa) software adapter on the Linux runners. The GPU path ran on Metal (macOS) and on WARP (Windows).\n- A real device-lost event. The callback code is in `shared.rs`, but no test forces a device loss.\n- A wasm32 build of the crate.\n- No production caller uses the kernel yet. The wiring into the app is #2621.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #3304 (zh-CN i18n draft) changes the root `Cargo.toml` (the workspace member list and the workspace dependencies) and `crates/ui/Cargo.toml` (the dependency list). It adds different lines. Whichever PR merges second refreshes.\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nChangelog: The new `camcraft-gpu` crate gives headless GPU compute to the CLI, MCP and tests. It has a capability probe, one cached device, the `CAMCRAFT_GPU_COMPUTE=off` switch, a CPU fallback with a logged reason, and a facet binning kernel with parity tests.\n\nRefs #3336\nFixes #2620\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
